This implementation implements bcrypt, which is the current standard for password hashing. It generates a 256-bit secure hash, stores it in a salt, and then encrypts it using a 128-bit key. If an attacker tries to guess your password, they must brute-force that key length and the salt, which is computationally infeasible on modern hardware.

